<h1>Results</h1>
This is the expected output for `mpirun -n 4 ./distributed-multigrid-reuse`:

@code{.cpp}

Num rows in matrix: 10000
Num ranks: 4

 iter      residual     setup    setup time  cg iters
    0             1  generate    0.00953173        27
    1       4.92756    record    0.00497701        37
    2      0.591079     reuse    0.00350611        27
    3      0.337404     reuse     0.0032835        29
    4     0.0844591     reuse    0.00333143        25
    5      0.023152     reuse    0.00330655        23
    6    0.00508051     reuse    0.00333697        21
    7   0.000999056     reuse    0.00331201        19
    8   0.000174637     reuse    0.00327568        16
    9   2.76182e-05     reuse    0.00329311        13
   10    3.9894e-06     reuse    0.00334166        11

Picard iterations: 11
Final residual: 5.31104e-07
Total setup time: 0.0444958
Total cg iterations: 248

@endcode

The first iteration uses generate(), the second one records the hierarchy, and the later ones reuse it.
With a refresh_interval of 1, every iteration after the first one records a new hierarchy, which takes about 0.005 seconds instead of 0.0033, while the Picard and Cg iteration counts stay the same.
The timings may vary depending on the machine.
